post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Aether is installed under /etc/xdg/quickshell/aether. It can coexist with
caelestia-shell-git; only one of the two shells should be running.

== Step 1: the Hyprland config (the settings pages need it) ==

    aether hypr install

That links this package's config into ~/.config/hypr and moves whatever was
there to ~/.config/hypr.aether-backup.<timestamp>. Nothing is deleted:
    mv ~/.config/hypr.aether-backup.<timestamp> ~/.config/hypr
puts the old config back.

Why it is required: every page under Nexus > Hyprland writes
~/.config/aether/hypr-vars.lua, and only this config reads that file. Without
it the pages save settings that never reach Hyprland. The Nexus page says so
too, until it is installed.

Keep your own tweaks in ~/.config/aether/hypr-user.lua -- the config loads it
last, and Nexus > Hyprland > User configuration opens it. Port what you still
need from the backup there, then delete the backup.

Log out and back in (or run `hyprctl reload`) after installing.

== Step 2: the shell ==

Hyprland starts it: the config from step 1 already calls `aether shell -d`.
To drive it by hand:
    aether shell -d         start
    aether shell -r -d      restart the running copy
    aether shell -l         tail the log
    aether shell -s         list every IPC target and function

== Where things live ==

Settings:  ~/.config/aether/shell.json
State:     ~/.local/state/aether
Data:      ~/.local/share/aether

On first start ~/.config/caelestia, ~/.local/state/caelestia and
~/.local/share/caelestia are copied once to the aether names. The old
directories are left alone, so a caelestia-shell install keeps its own.

The installed config already sets SSH_ASKPASS, SUDO_ASKPASS and
QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME; do not export them by hand. SSH still prompts in the
terminal when one is attached -- set SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE=force if you want the
dialog everywhere.

The shell itself writes only ~/.config/aether/. It never edits
~/.config/hypr; `aether hypr install` is the one command that does.

Optional extras:
    hyprmoncfg                   saved monitor layouts (Display page)
    bluez                        Bluetooth and the pairing agent
    fprintd / howdy-next         fingerprint / face unlock
    xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland  screen sharing and file pickers
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Aether was updated. Restart the running copy:

    aether shell -r -d

If Nexus > Hyprland shows a warning that the config is not installed, run:

    aether hypr install

Your settings in ~/.config/aether are kept.
EOF
}

pre_remove() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Aether's configuration is kept in ~/.config/aether/ and is not removed by
this package. Delete it yourself if you also want to drop your settings.

~/.config/hypr holds symlinks into this package after `aether hypr install`.
Remove them (or restore a backup from ~/.config/hypr.aether-backup.*) before
uninstalling, or Hyprland will start with a config that points at nothing.
EOF
}
